From 13634f9a0d9cf6ca5332dd2a707e48dd9c02302b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:17:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(compiler): reject explicit zero VARCHAR/NVARCHAR length
 instead of using 4096

- CubridTypeCompiler.visit_VARCHAR / visit_NVARCHAR tested the length by
  truthiness, so String(0) / VARCHAR(0) / NVARCHAR(0) compiled to the
  VARCHAR(4096) / NCHAR VARYING(4096) default (#440)
- length=None still renders the documented default; an explicit 0 now
  raises CompileError because CUBRID has no zero-length VARCHAR
- add regression tests for String, Unicode, VARCHAR and NVARCHAR with
  length=0, plus String() keeping the default
- note the behavior in docs/TYPES.md (en/ko), CHANGELOG and llms-full.txt

Closes #440
---
